data list_literal_has_no_lowered_form: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "list_literal_has_no_lowered_form" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "a list literal `[e1, .., en]` has no lowered form in v2 body lowering, on ANY route: `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_primary_expr` answered it with `body_lower_pattern_first_atom_optional`, its first atom, the `[` token, so every element reached no reference site -- a silent drop in data initializers, let values, and call arguments alike (DESIGN section 5)",
    "HOW IT SURFACED, 2026-09-23. gunbc#12145 stopped the operand reader narrowing a sequence to its left element; a list-literal call argument then answered Absent and refused its whole module as `body_lowering_reason_call_argument_unread`. gunbc#12173 kept that refusal but LOCATED it: a list literal anywhere in a call argument value refuses at the list with `body_lowering_reason_list_literal_unlowered` (ruling C of the XL-2 lane) -- reading the argument would otherwise have traded a loud refusal for the silent drop above. Four modules main accepted then refused, because main's data-initializer route had been dropping a list inside a call argument silently. Witness: `v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.call_argument_value_resolve_refusal`.",
    "EXPOSED, NOT INTRODUCED: the parent of gunbc#12145 (2de78893dfe) accepted this shape only by SILENT NARROWING -- the operand reader answered a sequence with its left element -- so the refusal on main after gunbc#12173 is a pre-existing defect made visible, not a new regression. Found by the XL-2 three-baseline identity census on gunbc#12194 (321 paths: 18 refusing at 2de78893dfe, 167 at ada85b9452, 101 after gunbc#12173).",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor on the routes that drop silently; mitigated (a located refusal) on the call-argument route since gunbc#12173. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- a list literal lowers whole to the existing `std.algebra` FreeMonoid concept or refuses, with no first-atom reading. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: list literals lower on EVERY route (call arguments, data initializers, let values) to a form whose elements reach the reference-site collector, so that no route answers a list with a proper part of it. The preferred form is the `Cons`/`Empty` construct chain through `v2.std.node_query` `construct_node`, pending a measurement of whether those tags resolve without an import on the census route.",
    "CLIMBED BY gunbc#12208 (MQ-1), THE TRIGGER'S CAPABILITY: one producer, `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_list_literal`, reached from `body_lower_primary_expr` through the value reader every position uses (`body_lower_value_lowered`), so call arguments, data initializers, let values, operands and scrutinees all get it -- no route answers a list with a proper part of it. Each element lowers whole; one that cannot refuses at the element (`body_lowering_reason_list_element_unlowered`). The call-argument refusal `body_lowering_reason_list_literal_unlowered` is deleted with its route. THE FORM IS NOT THE CONSTRUCT CHAIN this row preferred: by parent and v2 Foundation ruling, a list literal lowers to ordinary calls over the `v2.std.algebra` free-monoid operations -- `[]` freemonoid_empty(), `[e]` freemonoid_singleton(item: e) (the generator embedding, declared once beside freemonoid_empty), longer lists a right-nested list_append over singletons -- each head the declaring qualified name, so resolve binds it by path rather than by a bare `Cons`/`Empty` tag whose import-free resolution was the open measurement above. Measured on srv1 at the PR head: the seven canary's 35 `list_literal_unlowered` paths cleared with no new refusal cause; a first-element-only mutation reds the shape claims and the conservation control. RESIDUAL, A DECLARED FRONTIER: eval and translate consuming the lowered calls end to end is not yet exercised; a closure without `v2.std.algebra` refuses the head at resolve, located.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.call_argument_value_resolve_refusal", decl_name: "a_named_list_argument_reaches_resolve", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.call_argument_value_resolve_refusal", decl_name: "a_positional_list_argument_reaches_resolve", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.call_argument_value_resolve_refusal", decl_name: "a_list_inside_a_nested_call_argument_reaches_resolve", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.call_argument_value_resolve_refusal", decl_name: "a_list_inside_a_record_literal_argument_reaches_resolve", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.list_literal_value_lowering", decl_name: "a_list_of_calls_lowers_every_call_whole_in_order", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.list_literal_value_lowering", decl_name: "a_nested_list_lowers_each_inner_list_whole_in_order", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.list_literal_value_lowering", decl_name: "an_empty_list_argument_lowers_to_freemonoid_empty", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.list_literal_value_lowering", decl_name: "a_list_argument_lowers_every_element_in_order", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.list_literal_value_lowering", decl_name: "a_list_argument_is_not_its_first_element_or_a_truncation", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.reference_conservation", decl_name: "a_list_literal_call_argument_conserves_every_element_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
